                <invention-title lang="de">SYSTEME UND VERFAHREN ZUR VERBESSERUNG DER AUSGANGSSTABILITÄT EINES HOCHFREQUENZLEISTUNGSVERSTÄRKERS</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">SYSTÈMES ET PROCÉDÉS POUR AMÉLIORER LA STABILITÉ DE SORTIE D'UN AMPLIFICATEUR DE PUISSANCE RADIOFRÉQUENCE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">SYSTEMS AND METHODS FOR IMPROVING OUTPUT STABILITY OF A RADIO FREQUENCY POWER AMPLIFIER</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present disclosure directs to a system and method for improving output stability of a radio frequency power amplifier (RFPA). The system may comprise a first processing circuit that is configured to: obtain an initial radio frequency signal (501, 601) to be amplified by the RFPA; determine a first compensation quantity based on a supply voltage of the RFPA (207, 610) and an output power of the RFPA (207, 610); determine a second compensation quantity based on the output power and a transistor junction temperature of the RFPA (207, 610); determine a gain compensation quantity based on the first compensation quantity and the second compensation quantity; generate a compensated radio frequency signal by performing, based on the gain compensation quantity, a gain compensation operation for the initial radio frequency signal; and transmit the compensated radio frequency signal to the RFPA (207, 610) for amplification.</p>
            </abstract>
